  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Shattered-Spire Assault was the defining military engagement of the Orca Incursion — a coordinated attack on Aurora Stack, the crystalline surface colony of Aurora Berg, led by the orca war-commander Gnarkzund Zaith. It resulted in the destruction of the Stack's eastern ridge, the death of Gnarkzund Zaith, the loss of an unknown number of penguin defenders, and the permanent corruption of the lower terraces' ice-memory. The assault is classified in orca sources under an older name — *gore-ruin* — which the earliest chronicle account preserves.
    
    ## The Assault
    
    Gnarkzund Zaith committed seven pods in staggered formation: lean raiders forward to draw defensive response, unmarked shamans following with blood-chants, warriors positioned between in what orca tactical tradition calls the ambush posture. The assault leveraged three principal weapons in combination. **Slide Prism**, a barrier-breaking technique, turned the Stack's crystal defenses inside-out — accounts describe penguins falling through their own fortifications. **Star∴eternal** fractured the colony's light-based defenses with such intensity that survivors reportedly flinch at reflected light on ice. The orca blood-magic technique **Rupture-Song** served a shore-breaker role, its concussive force shattering ice fortifications the Stack was never built to absorb; during the third wave, its collective variant **Khrrak's Collapse** was deployed against the eastern settlement, causing defenders to collapse from internal hemorrhaging without external trauma.
    
    The Wake-Singers — orca shamanic practitioners — focused their hunt-songs through the **Dreaming Tooth**, an artifact of pressure-magic, weaponizing the Stack's own crystalline architecture. Spires cracked along harmonic lines. Three terraces fell inward. The aurora stuttered until the colony's light-based defenses failed entirely.
    
    The assault was, as one account puts it, a siege wearing a raid's skin. The defenders' counter-tactics had been designed for the former, not the latter.
    
    ## Defense and Culmination
    
    The **Midnight Claws**, the syndicate that controlled Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy, and operatives of the **☽'shadow Covens' Order** held the lower eastern corridors under Flipper Accord defense obligations. Fire-core reserves were critically depleted by the final hours. Among the weapons wielded in defense was the **Radiant Ring**, an aurora-glass war-hammer whose fracture widened with each strike.
    
    The engagement ended when the Midnight Claws and shadow Covens practitioners cast **Grulkzul Omega Strike**, an unprecedented blood-working that fused Nightshelf fire-knowledge with orca pressure-magic techniques. The spell caused a violent decompression that destroyed the entire eastern ridge, killing Gnarkzund Zaith and silencing the shamans' wake-chanting. The casters did not survive in any conventional sense — accounts describe their consciousness dispersing across the frozen deep. How Nightshelf practitioners came to possess sufficient command of orca pressure-magic to improvise such a working under battlefield conditions is a question the official record does not address.
    
    The duration of the assault is uncertain. Sources give three days or five. The Stack's time-crystals shattered with the eastern ridge, and no reliable temporal reference survived.
    
    ## Evidence of Internal Sabotage
    
    Evidence preserved in the **Thaw-Paths Medallion**, a relic later forced to reveal its deeper pathways, indicated that the eastern ridge's crystal barricades had been deliberately weakened from within before the assault. Tool-marks were precise enough to imply flippers that knew exactly which lenses to crack. One approach path encoded in the medallion's glass originated not from the sea but from within the Stack's council tier, along a maintenance corridor assigned to a senior official's patrol route. Chronicle accounts from the investigation of Shadow-Broker Nyla's confession identify this official as Council member **Amaang Skael'Compass**, though the connection was suppressed rather than prosecuted.
    
    ## Aftermath
    
    Side-channels used by the Wake-Singers became desecrated ground, their ice so corrupted that even fire-sutured senses cannot read what the stone remembers. A corruption scar scored into the ice-memory of the lower terraces has never been successfully cleansed. The unauthorized casting of Grulkzul Omega Strike — performed without Aurora Stack council approval — later became central to debates about hoarded knowledge and unaccountable acts.
    
    **Kael-the-Rememberer**, a survivor, still sets out two cups of fire-tea every dawn — one for a sister who died in the assault. No one drinks from the second.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771585162519_0", anchor: "The Shattered-Spire Assault was the defining military engagement of the Orca Incursion", text: "The entry omits what the deep ice suggests because the deep ice only suggests it. Stratum records from the cycle preceding the assault show Aurora harvesting teams operating beyond the traditional ice-shelf boundary — into waters the orca had used as calving grounds for generations. Penguin tool-marks in orca territory, unmistakable. I cannot prove causation. But I have found this pattern twice before in raids the chronicles treat as unprovoked, and both times the ice showed encroachment first. Note that the word 'unprovoked' appears nowhere in my text. I want the reader to notice I did not use it.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585162519_1", anchor: "How Nightshelf practitioners came to possess sufficient command of orca pressure-magic", text: "The question answers itself if you read the Midnight Claws' operational history without blinking. They ran the deep tunnels for thirty winters. The deep tunnels border the pressure-zones. Wake-Singers desecrated at least two of those tunnels during the Incursion, leaving residue any sufficiently desperate practitioner could study. And the Nightshelf intelligence operations I referenced in my Otrolal annotation did not limit themselves to defensive coordination. 'Improvise under battlefield conditions' is what you write when you do not want to say *had been preparing for years.*", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585162519_2", anchor: "the loss of an unknown number of penguin defenders", text: "Not unknown. Unknowable. The corruption scar destroyed the ice-memory that would have recorded the deaths. Oral accounts collected decades later give figures ranging from forty to three hundred — not a margin of error but a confession that no one was counting.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585162519_3", anchor: "suppressed rather than prosecuted", text: "The maintenance corridor is still accessible. The tool-marks are still there. Someone filed them down but did not fill them — the kind of suppression that hopes no one looks, not the kind that destroys evidence. I looked.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585162519_4", anchor: "No one drinks from the second.", text: "Kael lives on the rebuilt western terrace. The fire-tea she uses comes from Nightshelf trade-stock — the same supply chain the Claws once controlled, the same trade the Flipper Accord guarantees. Every morning she pours warmth purchased with the treaty her sister died defending. She has never mentioned this to anyone who has written it down.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
